: \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3f320efdf91cd561478cb9198eebdd7e9726f22c39eee33f2937be1b852cd0b2","event_uuid":"e64e1b74-dba7-4acc-b57a-1296205fe21e","position":{"commit_sha":"a5bd126ff0ed6c8faaf6300fe7a188d95d20ed73","position":"1786809404926290001-e64e1b74-dba7-4acc-b57a-1296205fe21e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"280933dfd6dece3471ccd0a00cccfb9f7d39087a9ac5c32142d048de74bcf8f1","event_uuid":"ac187b19-d9c7-4860-b8d4-b8b92411b045","position":{"commit_sha":"a5bd126ff0ed6c8faaf6300fe7a188d95d20ed73","position":"1786809405854491001-ac187b19-d9c7-4860-b8d4-b8b92411b045"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ab4f16ef237e47ff61605bb3ce326072f0b4e0298a76d343fd2c4df3d35ce925","event_uuid":"2c84f7c2-0b7c-4c17-85b2-1e4e44e2ec79","position":{"commit_sha":"a0ec5d6d01ce12ac6ae7caee6179cfdea6929cc6","position":"1786814205598047001-2c84f7c2-0b7c-4c17-85b2-1e4e44e2ec79"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented in worktree impl-a01d-fanout. Extracted _fetch_project(client, queries) (symmetric to _enrich_project): drains both base queries for one project into a LOCAL list, merged into the shared snapshot ONLY on success (atomic — no partial/empty read leaks as deletions). Per-project try/except in _build_snapshot: transport error -> emit fetcher-project-fetch-failed alert (project + pass_id) + CONTINUE; SilentTruncationError/BackendPaginationStallError re-raise (fail loud); invalid key still fails closed in jql_active (626d). Single-project path (len==1: one key / unseeded fallback) fails CLOSED unchanged so it never writes an empty all-deletions snapshot (AC #3 regression parity; existing single-project + truncation-gate tests still pass). Added always-on unit test_one_project_base_query_failure_does_not_abort_pass (BAD raises HTTPError, OK returns issues): RED before fix, GREEN after; mutation check (revert isolation -> re-raise) returns RED. make lint + make typecheck clean; fetcher.py trimmed to 650 lines (module-size AC). One unrelated pre-existing env failure state/test_ref_lock.py::test_ac0_blob_ref_roundtrips_through_remote (git cat-file exit 128 on temp bare repo) — reproduces on pristine origin/main.","timestamp":1786814205598047001}],"created_at":1786807235871094001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8ac9dc77-b6a5-4d75-a021-4e50128dbabc","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"05b8-4efe-8d58-4c27"}],"description":"## Problem\nThe reconciler multi-project fan-out (story 1734) runs every mapped project's base\n(active + done-recent) JQL queries in a single flat loop with NO per-project error\nisolation: `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py` `_build_snapshot` builds\n`queries` across all projects and iterates `for jql, cap in queries:` — any single\nproject's transport failure (ACLI 400 unknown-project, 401/403 permission, 404,\n429 rate-limit, 5xx, timeout) propagates out and ABORTS THE ENTIRE PASS for all\nprojects. The enrichment loop directly below already fails open per-project\n(`_enrich_project` \"each pass failing open independently so a per-project fault\ndegrades only that project\"). The base-query loop never inherited that resilience.\n\nThis is the PROVEN root cause of the 2026-08-15 production outage (bug\n05b8-4efe-8d58-4c27): a single mapped-but-nonexistent project key (`LEG`) —\nsyntactically valid, so `_validate_project_key` passes — made ACLI exit 1 and took\ndown ~12h of scheduled Reconcile Bridge passes across every project.\n\n## Approach\nExtract a `_fetch_project(client, proj, pass_id, repo_root, alert_store)` helper\n(symmetric to `_enrich_project`) that drains BOTH base queries (active +\ndone-recent) for one project into a LOCAL dict and returns it. `_build_snapshot`\ncalls it inside a per-project try/except and merges the returned dict into the\nshared `snapshot`/`seen_keys` ONLY on success. This makes the no-partial-merge\ncontract true by construction: a transport failure mid-pagination of the active\nquery, or after the active query merged but the done-recent query fails, discards\nthat project's LOCAL dict entirely — no partial keys ever reach the shared snapshot\nwhere the differ would read them as deletions.\n\nOn a per-project transport error the boundary emits an observable alert via\n`alert_store.append({\"kind\": \"fetcher-project-fetch-failed\", \"project\": <key>,\n\"pass_id\": pass_id, ...})`, discards the local dict, and CONTINUEs to the other\nprojects. Preserve the existing fail-CLOSED behavior for a\nsyntactically-invalid/absent key: `jql_active`/`jql_done_recent` call\n`_validate_project_key` OUTSIDE the per-project try (bug 626d intent unchanged) so a\nbad key still aborts the pass. Preserve the re-raise of `BackendPaginationStallError`\n(a stalled pager is a truncated whole-project read and must still surface),\nmatching the enrichment loop's exception handling exactly. Keep the dedup\n(`seen_keys`) and the `fetcher-dedup-suppressed` alert behavior intact — dedup now\nruns at the atomic merge of each project's local dict.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] One mapped project's base-query transport error does not abort the pass; the other projects' issues still land in the snapshot, and NO partial keys from the failed project are merged. Verified by the new unit `test_one_project_base_query_failure_does_not_abort_pass` in `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_multi_project.py`.\n- [ ] A per-project base-query fetch failure emits an observable `fetcher-project-fetch-failed` alert naming the project and pass_id. Verified: the new unit asserts a matching record in `bridge_state/bridge_alerts/*.jsonl`.\n- [ ] The single-project (unseeded store) path remains regression-identical. Verified: the existing `test_single_project_fallback_is_regression_identical` still passes.\n- [ ] A syntactically-invalid/absent key still fails closed (626d preserved) and a `BackendPaginationStallError` still re-raises. Verified: `_validate_project_key` is still called by `jql_active`/`jql_done_recent` outside the per-project try, and the boundary re-raises `BackendPaginationStallError` exactly as `_enrich_project` does.\n\n## Testing\nAdd an always-on unit (no live Jira) to `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_multi_project.py`\nusing a `_FakeClient` whose `search_issues` RAISES for project `BAD` (e.g. an\n`HTTPError`/ACLI error) but returns issues for `OK`; assert `OK`'s issues land in\nthe snapshot, the pass is not aborted, and the `fetcher-project-fetch-failed` alert\nfired for `BAD`. This is the always-on regression the incident lacked (closes the\nP0-3 test gap). Mutation check: reverting the per-project try/except returns the\ntest to RED. Run with\n`python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_multi_project.py -q`,\nplus `make lint` and `make typecheck`.\n\n## Sequencing\nEdits `fetcher.py` `_build_snapshot` base-query region. Ticket C (non-Done status)\nalso edits `fetcher.py` — C is sequenced AFTER this ticket to avoid conflict.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py","reason":"Add per-project fail-open boundary around the base-query fan-out loop in _build_snapshot"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_multi_project.py","reason":"Always-on unit: one project raises, another succeeds; assert isolation + alert"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"e64e1b74-dba7-4acc-b57a-1296205fe21e","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"a01d-b024-49dd-4254","ticket_type":"task","title":"Reconciler fan-out: per-project resilience in base-query loop (no whole-pass abort on one bad project)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d3df1e85-68dd-478b-9db5-a76b684d3fca","3c3556ea-21b1-409e-a687-6cd699dcf40b","59d7522a-325b-44c5-be0f-c9a14954b751","8ac9dc77-b6a5-4d75-a021-4e50128dbabc","1e84733b-4d5c-46e9-bec6-2eee3ffe89f6","c212ddb5-4299-456e-9f69-723ec9fd107b","cc2c0bb2-fc71-46b2-9628-68c7a67a7ce2","e64e1b74-dba7-4acc-b57a-1296205fe21e","ac187b19-d9c7-4860-b8d4-b8b92411b045","2c84f7c2-0b7c-4c17-85b2-1e4e44e2ec79"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786814205598047002,"uuid":"f9ad9570-87ce-4cfd-ac77-8f2b444c4f07"}